When generating a Git commit message for this repository, use Conventional Commits.

Format, one subject line under 100 characters:

type: short imperative description

Pick the type from the change:

- feat: a new feature
- fix: a bug fix
- docs: documentation only
- style: formatting or whitespace, no behavior change
- refactor: a code change that is not a fix or a feature
- perf: a performance improvement
- test: tests only
- build: the build system or dependencies
- ci: CI configuration
- chore: maintenance that fits none of the types above

Rules:

- Lowercase type, then a colon and a single space
- Imperative present tense, for example "add", "fix", or "update"
- No trailing period
- English
- Do not list files or restate the diff line by line
- Add a body only when the reason is not obvious from the subject

Examples:

- fix: correct workout stat calculation
- feat: add weekly progress chart
- chore: ignore local editor settings
